lculate the LTE for step $n$ starting at $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{τ}_{n} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-({y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)+Δy) \\\\  & =[5x+5\\cdot Δx]-[5x+5\\cdot Δx] \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323879 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323880 13194139534973 true] [17592186323879 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323881 13194139534973 true] [17592186323879 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323882 13194139534973 true] [17592186323879 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323883 13194139534973 true] [17592186323879 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323884 13194139534973 true] [17592186323879 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534973 true] [17592186323879 1041 "selection" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323879 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323883 13194139534973 true] [17592186323879 1110 #uuid "9d4b7b84-26c4-541b-8c5f-70c2c42994dc" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323880 1034 "Δx" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323880 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323880 1111 #uuid "62f8bb6e-91c8-58f1-9031-b312cd765ec8" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323881 1034 "5\\cdot (Δx)^{2}" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323881 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323881 1111 #uuid "1807d7ca-570f-581e-b357-11115cd0a39d" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323882 1034 "5x+5\\cdot Δx" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323882 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323882 1111 #uuid "faa08d70-9367-5369-a475-db1de7a6a7bf" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323883 1034 "0" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323883 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323883 1111 #uuid "62312486-2c44-520b-8020-06fc4957ced8" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323884 1034 "5\\cdot Δx" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323884 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323884 1111 #uuid "a00dbdbf-7c51-5dc2-a97c-6706c28c18a8" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323885 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323886 13194139534973 true] [17592186323885 1089 "q-333498" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323885 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534973 true] [17592186323885 1100 "Suppose we wish to approximate the solution to an initial value problem using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf the exact solution is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)=\\frac{1}{x},$ find an expression for the local truncation error for the step from $x$ to ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx.$" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323885 1113 #uuid "bae6a64b-b976-5114-bc74-05b9d6b499d3" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323885 1145 "The local truncation error (LTE) is the error made in a single step of a numerical method, when the step begins from an exact value. The LTE of a numerical method at step $n$ from $x$ with exact value ${y}_{\\text{exact}}$ to ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{τ}_{n} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-({y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)+Δy).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that the exact solution of the initial value problem is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Now, let's find the $y$-increment given by the numerical method.\n\nFirst, the slope at a step starting at $x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{exact}}^{′}(x)={(\\frac{1}{x})}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the increment given by the numerical method is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}^{′}(x)\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the exact value at ${x}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}}) & =({y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)+Δx) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x+Δx}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the LTE for step $n$ starting at $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{τ}_{n} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-({y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)+Δy) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x+Δx}-(\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot Δx)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323