} \\\\  & =[{x}^{2}+4x+5+(2x+4)\\cdot Δx+(Δx)^{2}]-[{x}^{2}+4x+5+({x}^{2}+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+5})\\cdot Δx] \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-{x}^{2}+4x-4x+5-5+(2x+4)\\cdot Δx+(Δx)^{2}-({x}^{2}+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+5})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =((2x+4)-{x}^{2}-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+5})\\cdot Δx+(Δx)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323908 13194139534973 true] [17592186323907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323909 13194139534973 true] [17592186323907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323910 13194139534973 true] [17592186323907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323911 13194139534973 true] [17592186323907 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323912 13194139534973 true] [17592186323907 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534973 true] [17592186323907 1041 "selection" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323907 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323909 13194139534973 true] [17592186323907 1110 #uuid "73cb0bbf-894c-54c6-8501-3c317d4b85eb" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323908 1034 "((2x+4)-{x}^{2}-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+5x+5})\\cdot Δx+(Δx)^{2}" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323908 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323908 1111 #uuid "c698b4ba-47ec-54c3-a865-3c67683d7d46" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323909 1034 "((2x+4)-{x}^{2}-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+5})\\cdot Δx+(Δx)^{2}" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323909 1111 #uuid "968c1317-39ac-508f-8591-d14035a66d93" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323910 1034 "((2x+5)-{x}^{2}-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+5})\\cdot Δx+(Δx)^{2}" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323910 1111 #uuid "4d425bbd-2de3-5c4b-930b-d2414e049c08" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323911 1034 "((2x+4)-{x}^{2}-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+4})\\cdot Δx+(Δx)^{2}" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323911 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323911 1111 #uuid "c500d8ba-d831-5674-bc20-104fc3014615" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323912 1034 "((2x+4)-x-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4x+5})\\cdot Δx+(Δx)^{2}" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323912 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323912 1111 #uuid "96e71f43-f8c1-5423-b2c6-205bd06e35f2" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323913 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323914 13194139534973 true] [17592186323913 1089 "q-334150" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323913 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534973 true] [17592186323913 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nSuppose we wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the exact solution is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)={e}^{x},$ compute the local truncation error ${τ}_{21}$ for the step starting at $x=1$ with step size $Δx=0.05.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n${τ}_{21}≈$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323913 1113 #uuid "528ea738-7281-5346-970a-6cb694f1ed20" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323913 1145 "The local truncation error (LTE) is the error made in a *single step* of a numerical method, when the step begins from an *exact value*. The LTE of a numerical method at step $n$ from $x$ with exact value ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)$ to ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{τ}_{n} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-({y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)+Δy).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that the exact solution is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)={e}^{x}.$ So, the $y$-value at the start of the step $x=1$ is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(1)=e.$\n\nNow, let's find the $y$-increment given by the numerical method.\n\nFirst, the slope at the start of the step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{exact}}^{′}(1) & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(1) \\\\  & =e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the increment at this step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}^{′}(1)\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =e\\cdot 0.05 \\\\  & =0.05e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the exact value at ${x}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(x+Δx) \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(1+0.05) \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(1.05) \\\\  & ={e}^{1.05}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the LTE for the step starting at $x=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{τ}_{21} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(1.05)-({y}_{\\text{exact}}(1)+Δy) \\\\  & ={e}^{1.05}-(e+0.05e) \\\\  & ={e}^{1.05}-1.05e \\\\  & ≈0.003\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323914 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323915 13194139534973 true] [17592186323914 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534973 true] [17592186323914 1041 "field-1" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323914 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323915 13194139534973 true] [17592186323914 1110 #uuid "e23ec364-9eab-5a53-9623-1654db04d22e" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323915 1034 "0.003" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323915 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323915 1111 #uuid "739b7864-a455-542a-886d-4763f80b8213" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323916 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323917 13194139534973 true] [17592186323916 1089 "q-334168" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323916 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534973 true] [17592186323916 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x+1,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSuppose we wish to approximate the solution using the following numerical method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{6}(x+{y}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the exact solution is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)={x}^{2}+x,$ compute the local truncation error, ${τ}_{6},$ for the step starting at $x=1$ with step size $Δx=0.2.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n${τ}_{6}≈$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323916 1113 #uuid "012e6ab9-3abc-5c2c-aa90-a9294d000bb2" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323916 1145 "The local truncation error (LTE) is the error made in a *single step* of a numerical method, when the step begins from an *exact value*. The LTE of a numerical method at step $n$ from $x$ with exact value ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)$ to ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{τ}_{n} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-({y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)+Δy).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that the exact solution is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)={x}^{2}+x.$ So, the $y$-value at the start of the step $x=1$ is ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(1)=2.$ Now, let's find the $y$-increment given by the numerical method.\n\nFirst, the slope at the start of the step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{exact}}^{′}(1) & =2(1)+1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the increment at this step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{6}(x+{y}_{\\text{exact}}^{′}(1))\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(1+3)\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & ≈0.1333.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the exact value at ${x}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(x+Δx) \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(1+0.2) \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(1.2) \\\\  & =(1.2)^{2}+1.2 \\\\  & =2.64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the LTE for the step starting at $x=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{τ}_{6} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(1.2)-({y}_{\\text{exact}}(1)+Δy) \\\\  & =2.64-(2+0.1333) \\\\  & ≈0.507\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323917 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323918 13194139534973 true] [17592186323917 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534973 true] [17592186323917 1041 "field-1" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323917 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323918 13194139534973 true] [17592186323917 1110 #uuid "60acfe35-bd52-5e4a-a3df-0e1d300afcea" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323918 1034 "0.507" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323918 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323918 1111 #uuid "76af2725-b392-5752-909e-0a4cb4cb233e" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323919 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323920 13194139534973 true] [17592186323919 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323922 13194139534973 true] [17592186323919 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323924 13194139534973 true] [17592186323919 1089 "q-334481" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323919 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534973 true] [17592186323919 1100 "A numerical method is used to approximate a solution to an initial value problem, resulting in the table below. If the exact solution is $y(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ find, rounded to three decimal places, the global truncation error at each step.\n\n| $n$ | ${x}_{n}$ | ${y}_{n}$ | ${e}_{n}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $0.1$ | $0.099$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $2$ | $0.3$ | $0.285$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $3$ | $0.6$ | $0.540$ | {{field-3}} |" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323919 1113 #uuid "f442655c-d19b-55c8-8144-02e2a27d866d" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323919 1145 "The global truncation error (GTE) is the total error accumulated after several steps of a numerical method. The GTE of a numerical method at step $n$ from ${x}_{n-1}$ to ${x}_{n}={x}_{n-1}+Δx$ is\n\n$$\n{e}_{n}=y({x}_{n})-{y}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $y({x}_{n})$ is the exact value at ${x}_{n},$ and ${y}_{n}$ is the numerical value produced after $n$ steps.\n\nWe are given the numerical values ${y}_{n}$ produced at each step in the table. Now, we compute the exact value $y({x}_{n})$ at each value of ${x}_{n}:$\n\n- The exact value at ${x}_{0}=0$ is $y(0)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)=0.$\n\n- The exact value at ${x}_{1}=0.1$ is $y(0.1)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.1).$\n\n- The exact value at ${x}_{2}=0.3$ is $y(0.3)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.3).$\n\n- The exact value at ${x}_{3}=0.6$ is $y(0.6)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.6).$\n\nLet's add these values to the table.\n\n| $n$ | ${x}_{n}$ | ${y}_{n}$ | $y({x}_{n})$ | ${e}_{n}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $0.1$ | $0.099$ | $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.1)$ |  |\n| $2$ | $0.3$ | $0.285$ | $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.3)$ |  |\n| $3$ | $0.6$ | $0.540$ | $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.6)$ |  |\n\nFinally, we find the GTE at each step, rounding to three decimal places in each case:\n\n- The GTE of the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}_{1} & =y({x}_{1})-{y}_{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.1)-0.099 \\\\  & ≈0.001.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The GTE of the second step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}_{2} & =y({x}_{2})-{y}_{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.3)-0.285 \\\\  & ≈0.011.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The GTE of the third step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}_{3} & =y({x}_{3})-{y}_{3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.6)-0.540 \\\\  & ≈0.025.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed table is as given below.\n\n| $n$ | ${x}_{n}$ | ${y}_{n}$ | $y({x}_{n})$ | ${e}_{n}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $0.1$ | $0.099$ | $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.1)$ | $0.001$ |\n| $2$ | $0.3$ | $0.285$ | $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.3)$ | $0.011$ |\n| $3$ | $0.6$ | $0.540$ | $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.6)$ | $0.025$ |" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323920 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323921 13194139534973 true] [17592186323920 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534973 true] [17592186323920 1041 "field-1" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323920 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323921 13194139534973 true] [17592186323920 1110 #uuid "6888e60b-b0b7-5e37-bf73-d677c8686b12" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323921 1034 "0.001" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323921 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323921 1111 #uuid "a480ca02-118e-5e4f-b9bf-259e6a45d4be" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323922 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323923 13194139534973 true] [17592186323922 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534973 true] [17592186323922 1041 "field-2" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323922 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323923 13194139534973 true] [17592186323922 1110 #uuid "3481225c-adba-5e37-898d-b871088c7075" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323923 1034 "0.011" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323923 1103 #edb/ref 1759218604