ced at each step in the table. Now, we compute the exact value $y({x}_{n})$ at each value of ${x}_{n}:$\n\n- The exact value at ${x}_{0}=0$ is $y(0)=\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}+1=1.$\n\n- The exact value at ${x}_{1}=0.2$ is $y(0.2)=\\frac{1}{2}(0.2)^{2}+1.$\n\n- The exact value at ${x}_{2}=0.4$ is $y(0.4)=\\frac{1}{2}(0.4)^{2}+1.$\n\n- The exact value at ${x}_{3}=0.7$ is $y(0.7)=\\frac{1}{2}(0.7)^{2}+1.$\n\nLet's add these values to the table.\n\n| $n$ | ${x}_{n}$ | ${y}_{n}$ | $y({x}_{n})$ | ${e}_{n}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $0.2$ | $1.010$ | $\\frac{1}{2}(0.2)^{2}+1$ |  |\n| $2$ | $0.4$ | $1.040$ | $\\frac{1}{2}(0.4)^{2}+1$ |  |\n| $3$ | $0.7$ | $1.140$ | $\\frac{1}{2}(0.7)^{2}+1$ |  |\n\nFinally, we find the GTE at each step, rounding to three decimal places in each case:\n\n- The GTE of the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}_{1} & =y({x}_{1})-{y}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0.2)^{2}+1-1.010 \\\\  & =0.010.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The GTE of the second step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}_{2} & =y({x}_{2})-{y}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0.4)^{2}+1-1.040 \\\\  & =0.040.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The GTE of the third step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}_{3} & =y({x}_{3})-{y}_{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0.7)^{2}+1-1.140 \\\\  & =0.105.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed table is as given below.\n\n| $n$ | ${x}_{n}$ | ${y}_{n}$ | $y({x}_{n})$ | ${e}_{n}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $0.2$ | $1.010$ | $\\frac{1}{2}(0.2)^{2}+1$ | $0.010$ |\n| $2$ | $0.4$ | $1.040$ | $\\frac{1}{2}(0.4)^{2}+1$ | $0.040$ |\n| $3$ | $0.7$ | $1.140$ | $\\frac{1}{2}(0.7)^{2}+1$ | $0.105$ |" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323927 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323928 13194139534973 true] [17592186323927 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323929 13194139534973 true] [17592186323927 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534973 true] [17592186323927 1041 "field-1" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323927 1104 #edb/ref 1759218632