itial value problem, resulting in the table below. If the exact solution is $y(x)=\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}},$ find, rounded to three decimal places, the global truncation error at each step.\n\n| $n$ | ${x}_{n}$ | ${y}_{n}$ | ${e}_{n}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $0.25$ | $1.030$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $2$ | $0.5$ | $1.100$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $3$ | $0.75$ | $1.230$ | {{field-3}} |" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323934 1113 #uuid "692557b6-3864-5ab2-8eff-c2021e9a265a" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323934 1145 "The global truncation error (GTE) is the total error accumulated after several steps of a numerical method. The GTE of a numerical method at step $n$ from ${x}_{n-1}$ to ${x}_{n}={x}_{n-1}+Δx$ is\n\n$$\n{e}_{n}=y({x}_{n})-{y}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $y({x}_{n})$ is the exact value at ${x}_{n},$ and ${y}_{n}$ is the numerical value produced after $n$ steps.\n\nWe are given the numerical values ${y}_{n}$ produced at each step in the table. Now, we compute the exact value $y({x}_{n})$ at each value of ${x}_{n}:$\n\n- The exact value at ${x}_{0}=0$ is $y(0)=\\sqrt{1+{0}^{2}}=1.$\n\n- The exact value at ${x}_{1}=0.25$ is $y(0.25)=\\sqrt{1+(0.25)^{2}}.$\n\n- The exact value at ${x}_{2}=0.5$ is $y(0.5)=\\sqrt{1+(0.5)^{2}}.$\n\n- The exact value at ${x}_{3}=0.75$ is $y(0.75)=\\sqrt{1+(0.75)^{2}}.$\n\nLet's add these values to the table.\n\n| $n$ | ${x}_{n}$ | ${y}_{n}$ | $y({x}_{n})$ | ${e}_{n}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $0.25$ | $1.030$ | $\\sqrt{1+(0.25)^{2}}$ |  |\n| $2$ | $0.5$ | $1.100$ | $\\sqrt{1+(0.5)^{2}}$ |  |\n| $3$ | $0.75$ | $1.230$ | $\\sqrt{1+(0.75)^{2}}$ |  |\n\nFinally, we find the GTE at each step, rounding to three decimal places in each case:\n\n- The GTE of the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}_{1} & =y({x}_{1})-{y}_{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+(0.25)^{2}}-1.030 \\\\  & ≈0.001.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The GTE of the second step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}_{2} & =y({x}_{2})-{y}_{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+(0.5)^{2}}-1.100 \\\\  & ≈0.018.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The GTE of the third step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}_{3} & =y({x}_{3})-{y}_{3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+(0.75)^{2}}-1.230 \\\\  & =0.020.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed table is as given below.\n\n| $n$ | ${x}_{n}$ | ${y}_{n}$ | $y({x}_{n})$ | ${e}_{n}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $0.25$ | $1.030$ | $\\sqrt{1+(0.25)^{2}}$ | $0.001$ |\n| $2$ | $0.5$ | $1.100$ | $\\sqrt{1+(0.5)^{2}}$ | $0.018$ |\n| $3$ | $0.75$ | $1.230$ | $\\sqrt{1+(0.75)^{2}}$ | $0.020$ |" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323935 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323936 13194139534973 true] [17592186323935 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323937 13194139534973 true] [17592186323935 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534973 true] [17592186323935 1041 "field-1" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323935 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323937 13194139534973 true] [17592186323935 1110 #uuid "51dd18ac-ef30-51f3-ab2d-a88877cb35d0" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323936 1034 "-0.001" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323936 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323936 1111 #uuid "618d3038-1117-5a24-bdcb-754cedc13265" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323937 1034 "0.001" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323937 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323937 1111 #uuid "10efe5b7-d142-51c0-a31d-85609e8d592c" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323938 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323939 13194139534973 true] [17592186323938 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534973 true] [17592186323938 1041 "field-2" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323938 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323939 13194139534973 true] [17592186323938 1110 #uuid "c36e8055-f017-5deb-9b79-cd0fa003c6bf" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323939 1034 "0.018" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323939 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534973 true] [17592186323939 1111 #uuid "c71470cb-6ce3-56a8-9168-9d8791343d19" 13194139534973 true] [17592186323940 1000 #edb/ref 1